        <body>
            <div xml:id="d337">

                <pb facs="0424" n="326" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg326"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94 Commission/521</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain (Mellon) to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 469</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-11-03">November 3, 1932</date>.<lb/>[Received November
                        11.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to forward herewith, as of
                    interest to the Department, copies of two memoranda prepared after a discussion
                    with Lord Lytton in the office of Sir John Simon in the House of Commons on
                    October 26, 1932, Mr. Norman Davis and Mr. Ray Atherton likewise being
                    present.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>(For the Ambassador)<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ray
                            Atherton</hi></signed><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Counselor of
                        Embassy</hi></closer>



